        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep bundle LSP tool names provider-safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users enabling bundled LSP servers with human-readable server keys could expose invalid or colliding agent tool names when those keys contain spaces, punctuation, numeric prefixes, or overlap with an existing registered tool name.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe bundle LSP runtime now keeps the original server key for user-facing labels and execution details while deriving a provider-safe model-facing tool prefix for hover, definition, and references tools. The prefix is bounded to the existing 64-character tool-name budget and disambiguated against sibling LSP prefixes plus already registered tool names, matching the bundle MCP naming boundary without changing configuration, provider routing, or LSP protocol behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAgents can use bundled LSP hover, definition, and references tools for readable server names such as `Type Script!` or numeric keys, and LSP tools are no longer dropped when the sanitized name would collide with a registered tool.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: at current head `56c777b8eb4ff413375ef20116a57b3a5b236410`, bundled LSP tool materialization keeps unsafe and colliding server keys provider-safe and unique while preserving the original server label in execution details.\n- Merge-conflict repair: merged current `upstream/main` into the PR branch and resolved the LSP test conflict by keeping the branch's injectable `MockChildProcess` capabilities while adopting main's `hoverProvider`, `definitionProvider`, and `referencesProvider` defaults.\n- Focused regression: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.test.ts` passed with 1 file and 14 tests.\n- Real behavior proof: GitHub `Real behavior proof` passed on current head `56c777b8eb4ff413375ef20116a57b3a5b236410`: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29243186902/job/86793828557\n- Targeted format: `node_modules\\.bin\\oxfmt.CMD --check --threads=1 src\\agents\\agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.ts src\\agents\\agent-bundle-lsp-runtime.test.ts` passed.\n- Diff hygiene: `git diff --check`, `git diff --cached --check`, and `git diff --check HEAD~1..HEAD` passed after the merge-conflict repair.\n- Duplicate search: no open self PR with the same root cause; `bundle LSP tool name` and `lsp_hover` open PR searches were empty, and `agent-bundle-lsp-runtime` only found adjacent LSP lifecycle/size PRs rather than a tool-name fix.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the bundle LSP runtime path, sibling bundle MCP naming helper, focused regression coverage, and current-head merge-conflict repair.",
